&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;100% Remote in Poland&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;This can be structured as a B2B contract or as an Employment Contract with full benefits.&lt;br&gt;Salary: &amp;nbsp;$117,000 - $133,000 + stock options.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Focal Systems builds AI camera networks for grocery retail. Hundreds of stores, major UK and European chains, and a customer list that keeps growing faster than most companies our size would attempt. The computer vision market is moving, and we&#39;re one of the few places actually deploying it at scale - not on slides, but in stores equipped with hundreds of shelf edge cameras that change how store teams do their jobs every shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Customer Integration team has taken every major retailer we&#39;ve signed through production — and as we add more customers, we’re looking for a senior engineer to lead high-quality deployments, own onboarding and integrations end-to-end, and help define how this function grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a real distributed AI system at scale — when a retailer&#39;s report is wrong, a pipeline is silently dropping events, task counts diverged somewhere between Kafka, Redis, MySQL, and MongoDB, you&#39;ll own the challenged end-to-end, not hand it off after one layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring new customers live — map their data formats to ours and validate pipelines held up at 10 stores before scaling up to 100 and then a 1000.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage live production configuration for dozens of active deployments — granular store configurations, feature flags and so on — where a single mistake can impact shelf monitoring across thousands of stores and be presented in a retailer&#39;s morning report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling that removes the manual work&amp;nbsp; — identify the patterns and build the systems that make the next deployment faster than the last one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with&amp;nbsp; customers when something goes wrong — explain what happened, own the fix, and close the loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll NOT Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the first line of technical support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; When a customer has a problem, you don&#39;t wait for it to get assigned.You’ll pick it up, see it through end-to-end,, and close the loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4+ years of hybrid experience&lt;/strong&gt;. You’ve written real production code and worked directly with external stakeholders. That could be integration or solutions engineering, a consultancy role with direct client work, freelancing on real production systems, or a technical role at a startup where you wore multiple hats. What matters is that you&#39;ve shipped code and been accountable to someone outside the engineering org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Python.&lt;/strong&gt; Pandas and NumPy are second nature. You default to an API-first mindset — designing clean contracts, composable interfaces, and avoiding&amp;nbsp; one-off scripts that don’t scale..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You can hold a complex distributed system in your head, decompose a messy customer problem into its parts, and come back with a solution — often one nobody else saw because they were&amp;nbsp; closest to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solid SQL and data work.&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnostic queries, tracing data inconsistencies, building ETL and transformation pipelines, following data across systems. You reach for SQL before you reach for a ticket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working knowledge of distributed systems&lt;/strong&gt;. Kafka, async pipelines, caching layers. You don&#39;t need to design them. You need to understand how they behave and figure out why data stopped flowing through them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear technical communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You can explain a root cause to a non-technical customer or stakeholder without jargon, and explain a customer&#39;s actual problem to an engineer without losing the detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GCP, Kubernetes, or Helm experience (reading configs and logs, not managing infrastructure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What we offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We care deeply about the health, happiness, and wellbeing of all of our employees. We offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Attractive Stock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Retreats&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education grants&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: Our pay bands are driven by market benchmarks in the target geography for hiring. Our posted ranges typically include multiple job levels. A candidate&#39;s level is determined by their performance throughout our talent acquisition process including technical screens, behavior interviews, presentations, work samples, and references. We will communicate transparently with the candidate at final stages regarding how we have leveled them, and what salary range that places them into. Placement within range is equally determined by education, general experience in your profession, specific experience in our domain, and your performance in the talent acquisition process. It is rare to receive an offer at the top of the range for a role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type: &lt;/strong&gt;Full-time, salaried employment&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote, United Kingdom only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;£90,000 - £105,000 + stock options.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Focal Systems is the industry leader in retail AI solutions. We are headquartered in San Francisco, California with operations in Canada and the UK, and a tech-hub in Poland. We are a Deep Learning first company. Our mission is to automate and optimize brick and mortar retail using deep learning computer vision. Focal Systems has been deployed at scale with some of the top retailers in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek smart, creative and passionate people who want to help build a great and enduring company and deploy Deep Learning to the world!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Responsible For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Manager, you will take ownership of how data is processed at Focal, and shape what that path becomes: from the imports that bring a retailer&#39;s planograms, inventory and store metadata into our platform, through the pipelines that turn them into signal, to the metrics and reports their head office acts on. You will work with data engineering, data scientists, analytics, customer success and the retailers themselves. What you build are data products, and the measure of one is what a retailer does differently because of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role. You will set direction and priorities as we roll out to hundreds of new stores, but you are also expected to know the systems well enough to be a partner in an engineering design conversation, pull your own numbers when something looks wrong, and hold a strong position in the discussions with customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a peer to the engineers you work with, someone who understands the systems well enough to know what is expensive and why and when to push back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are drawn to the seams between teams, where ownership is shared and the hardest problems live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write your own queries and interrogate the answers before anyone else has to, and you can name the business number a data product of yours moved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can change your mind in a technical argument, and you can point to the time you did&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong judgment about what not to build, and you have killed your own work when it stopped earning its place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI as part of how you actually work, and you have built things with it that other people went on to use, not demos you gave once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate complicated things crisply to people who do not share your context, including customers hearing an answer they did not want&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build things that outlast you, whether runbooks, tooling or documented decisions, because you would rather remove yourself as a dependency than be indispensable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product direction for the full data path, from how a retailer&#39;s data arrives to what our reports say, and set the priorities where the two ends pull against each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how customer data gets into Focal: imports, planograms, store metadata, cut-off configuration, and the chain-specific flows each retailer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own what comes out and whether anyone acts on it: the metrics, the reporting APIs, the insight-generating agents, and the customer-facing dashboards a head office runs its week on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery with retailers and store colleagues, and turn what you learn into a product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship, then find out whether anyone used it, and act on the answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate your own work with AI and share what you build with the rest of the product team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need to Be Successful&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product management, including real time on a technically deep product where you owned integrations, data, or both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical depth to reason about APIs, data pipelines and system boundaries, and to be an equal partner in an engineering discussion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building for a hierarchy of users who need different things from the same data: a store manager, a regional director and a head of supply chain reading one dataset three ways, served by one configurable surface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on comfort with SQL and the ability to answer your own data questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in the analytics and BI tooling landscape, and a view on what makes a dashboard worth returning to rather than merely correct&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of a product roadmap end to end, from problem definition through to something shipped and adopted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of getting things done across teams, and the communication to influence engineering and commercial partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with enterprise customers, including holding a position they disagree with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating remote-first, across a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel occasionally for store and customer visits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Would Set You Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with high-volume, noisy sensor or computer-vision data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with change data capture into a cloud warehouse (ideally Snowflake)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI-powered features, including the call on when a model is good enough to ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Focal Systems&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Focal Systems means becoming part of a company that&#39;s truly making a difference in the retail world. Here&#39;s why you should consider us:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Values and Mission: &lt;/strong&gt;We are a tightly-knit team with an ambitious mission and a strong set of core values, which define our approach to business and have successfully guided us since inception.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Team: &lt;/strong&gt;We are a team of hard-working, fun-loving professionals from some of the most eminent universities, research labs, and tech companies of our time. We pride ourselves on recruiting exceptional individuals to help us redefine the state-of-the-art.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outstanding Partners:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;We work with 10+ of the largest retailers in the world and have a world-class roster of investors, advisors and partners to support &amp;amp; advise us in our endeavours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care deeply about the health, happiness, and wellbeing of all of our employees. We offer:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Attractive Stock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development Budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position: Senior QA Engineer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;100% Remote in Poland&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;This can be structured as a B2B contract or as an Employment Contract with full benefits.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt; $75,000 - $95,000 + stock options&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.focal.systems/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Focal Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;is the industry leader in retail AI solutions. We are headquartered in San Francisco, California with operations in Canada and the UK, and a tech-hub in Poland. We are a Deep Learning first company. Our mission is to automate and optimize brick and mortar retail using deep learning computer vision. Focal Systems has been deployed at scale with some of the top retailers in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek smart, creative and passionate people who want to help build a great and enduring company and deploy Deep Learning to the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior QA Engineer who is curious, detail-oriented, and eager to build a career in quality engineering. You enjoy understanding how systems work, spotting issues others might miss, and learning how to improve product quality through testing and automation.&lt;br&gt;You’re a strong collaborator and communicator who enjoys working closely with engineers, product managers, and data teams. You’re motivated to learn modern QA tools and practices, especially around automation, APIs, and backend validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the team in ensuring the quality and reliability of our products across UI, APIs, and backend systems. You’ll gain hands-on experience with testing frameworks, automation tools, and data validation, while contributing to improving our overall quality standards.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additionally, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;GUI / API testing and backend validation&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure systems behave as expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineers to ensure quality coverage across frontend and backend features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bugs, document issues clearly, and support their resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously build your knowledge of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;QA best practices, tools, and automation strategies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
